===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:age|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂ey-|id=life}}
From {{inh|en|enm|age}}, {{der|en|fro|eage|aage, eage, edage}}, from an assumed {{der|en|la-vul|*aetāticum}}, derived from {{der|en|la|aetas|aetātem}}, itself derived from {{m|la|aevum||lifetime}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂eyu-||vital force}}. Compare {{cog|fr|âge}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|ieldu}}.

The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|agen}}, from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=9141202500}}</ref> Originally found mostly as a participial adjective, probably an adjective in {{m|enm|-ed}}, derived from the noun, reanalyzed to create a verb; perhaps modeled on such pairs as {{noncog|la|senēscō}} ({{m|la|seneō}}; verb) / {{m|la|senex|pos=adjective}} and {{cog|frm|vieillir|pos=verb}} / {{m|frm|vieil|pos=adjective}}. Also compare {{cog|fro|[[se]] [[aagier]]}}, {{m|fro|eogier|t=become of age}}.<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=āǧen|pos=v|id=MED827}}</ref>

