===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} The amount of time that some [[being#Noun|being]] has been alive, or that some thing has been in existence, as measured from its birth or origin until the present or until some other given reference point. (Often measured in [[number#Noun|number]] of [[year]]s;  alternatively in [[month]]s, [[day]]s, [[hour]]s, etc.; see also the usage notes)
#: {{ux|en|"What is the '''age''' of your oldest child?" — "He's ten." ''(ten years old)''}}
#: {{ux|en|What were their '''ages''' at the time of their marriage?}}
#: {{ux|en|We can determine the '''age''' of fossils using radiometric dating.}}
#: {{ux|en|What is the present '''age''' of the earth?}}
#: {{ux|en|Children of that '''age''' should be able to dress themselves.}}
#: {{ux|en|I have a daughter your '''age''', and I tell her when I was your '''age''' I was already working.}}
#: {{ux|en|You should play with kids the same '''age''' as you.}}
#: {{ux|en|At your '''age''', your mom and I'd already found a job.}}
#: {{ux|en|We both have kids under '''age''' four.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Peter Wilby|chapter=Finland’s education ambassador spreads the word|url=https://www.theguardian.com/education/2013/jul/01/education-michael-gove-finland-gcse|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170716042037/https://www.theguardian.com/education/2013/jul/01/education-michael-gove-finland-gcse|archivedate=16 July 2017|title=w:The Guardian|location=London|date=1 July 2013|chapter2=Finland spreads word on schools|title2=w:The Guardian Weekly|location2=London|date2=19 July 2013|volume2=189|issue2=6|page2=30|passage=Imagine a country where children do nothing but play until they start compulsory schooling at '''age''' seven. Then, without exception, they attend comprehensives until the '''age''' of 16. Charging school fees is illegal, and so is sorting pupils into ability groups by streaming or setting.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The state of being [[old]]; the latter part of life.
#: {{syn|en|old age|dotage|senility|seniority|Thesaurus:old age}}
#: {{ant|en|youth}}
#* '''1936 Feb. 15''', {{w|Ernest Hemingway}}, [https://books.google.com.hk/books?id=XfPa5B2blv0C&pg=PA202 letter] to {{w|Maxwell Perkins}}:
#*: Feel awfully about {{w|F. Scott Fitzgerald|Scott}}... It was a terrible thing for him to love youth so much that he jumped straight from youth to [[senility]] without going through [[manhood]]. The minute he felt youth going he was frightened again and thought there was nothing between youth and '''age'''.
#: {{ux|en|Wisdom doesn't necessarily come with '''age''', sometimes '''age''' just shows up all by itself.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any particular [[stage#Noun|stage]] of [[life]].
#: {{co|en|the '''age''' of infancy}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[time#Noun|time]] of life at which some particular [[power#Noun|power]] or [[capacity]] is [[understand|understood]] to become [[vested#Adjective|vested]].
#: {{co|en|the [[age of consent|'''age''' of consent]]; the [[age of discretion|'''age''' of discretion]]}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[maturity|Maturity]]; ''especially'', the time of life at which one [[attain]]s full [[personal#Adjective|personal]] rights and [[capacity|capacities]].
#: {{syn|en|majority|adulthood}}
#: {{co|en|to [[come of age|come of '''age''']]; she is now [[of age|of '''age''']]}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A particular period of time in [[history]], as distinguished from others.
#: {{syn|en|epoch|time|era|Thesaurus:era}}
#: {{co|en|the golden '''age''' of cinema; the first '''age''' of colonialism; a bygone '''age'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=May 9 1961|author=w:Newton Minow|title=w:Television and the Public Interest
|passage=Ours has been called the jet '''age''', the atomic '''age''', the space '''age'''. It is also, I submit, the television '''age'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1970|author=Jim Theis|title=The Eye of Argon|work=OSFAN|volume=10|page=33|section=Chapter 3½|url=https://ansible.uk/misc/eyeargon.pdf|passage=Encircling the marble altar was a congregation of leering shamen. Eerie chants of a bygone '''age''', originating unknown eons before the memory of man, were being uttered from the buried recesses of the acolytes' deep lings {{sic}}.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:National Geographic|year=1987|month=October|volume=172|number=4|title=Results of the Smell Survey|author=Avery N. Gilbert and Charles J. Wysocki|page=515
|text=A survey of this magnitude could only be undertaken in the computer '''age'''; analyzing the returns by hand would be impossible.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|title=Yesterday’s fuel: The world’s thirst for oil could be nearing a peak. That is bad news for producers, excellent for everyone else.|url=https://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21582516-worlds-thirst-oil-could-be-nearing-peak-bad-news-producers-excellent|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130801154742/http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21582516-worlds-thirst-oil-could-be-nearing-peak-bad-news-producers-excellent|archivedate=1 August 2013|date=3 August 2013|volume=408|issue=8847|passage=The dawn of the oil '''age''' was fairly recent. Although the stuff was used to waterproof boats in the Middle East 6,000 years ago, extracting it in earnest began only in 1859 after an oil strike in Pennsylvania. The first barrels of crude fetched $18 (around $450 at today’s prices). It was used to make kerosene, the main fuel for artificial lighting after overfishing led to a shortage of whale blubber.}}
## The time or era in history when someone or something was alive or flourished.
##: {{ux|en|the '''age''' of Pericles; the '''age''' of the dinosaurs}}
## {{lb|en|countable}} A [[great#Adjective|great]] period in the history of the [[Earth]].
##: {{ux|en|The [[Bronze Age|Bronze '''Age''']] was followed by the [[Iron Age|Iron '''Age''']].}}
## {{senseid|en|geology}}{{lb|en|countable|geology}} The shortest [[geochronologic]] [[unit]], being a period of [[thousand]]s to [[million]]s of [[year]]s; a [[subdivision]] of an [[epoch]] (or sometimes a [[subepoch]]).
##: {{ux|en|The Tithonian '''Age''' was the last in the Late Jurassic Epoch.}}
# {{lb|en|astrology}} One of the twelve [[division]]s of a [[Great Year]], equal to roughly 2000 years and governed by one of the [[zodiacal]] signs; a [[Platonic month]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=10 Apr 1911|journal= The Evening News|location=Sydney|page=8|column=2|text=Mr Lewis says we are living in the '''age''' of Aquarius, which means that the world is at present passing through the zodiacal sign of Aquarius, the airy constellation.}}
# {{senseid|en|century}} {{lb|en|countable}} A period of [[one]] [[hundred]] years; a [[century]].
#: {{syn|en|centennium}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncommon|possibly|dated}} A [[generation]].
#: {{ux|en|There are three '''ages''' living in her house.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|hyperbole}} A [[long]] time.
#: {{syn|en|eternity|yonks|Thesaurus:eon}}
#: {{ux|en|It’s been an '''age''' since we last saw you.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} [[lifespan|Lifespan]], [[lifetime]]; the total time that some being is alive from  birth to death (or some category of beings, on average).
#: {{ux|en|The '''age''' of man is three score years and ten.}}
#: {{ux|en|Thrice the '''age''' of a dog is that of a horse.}}
#: {{ux|en|Done at London, in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and ninety-five, in the fifty-eighth year of my '''age'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Physical Condition of Centenarians, as Derived from Personal Observation in Nine Genuine Examples|last=Duncan Gibb|first=George|location=London|year=1872|page=13|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=NGFijiOwclkC&pg=PA13|passage=The CHAIRMAN said if Lord Bacon had asserted that man's '''age''' exceeded that of all other living creatures, he must have included the patriarchs in his calculation. Without doubt the '''age''' of many animals exceeded that of man. [...] Indeed, if the assumed '''age''' of the patriarchs be correct, it is against our own experience, it being an admitted fact that the duration of human life has increased. The '''age''' of the patriarchs was by some attributed to the effect of certain waters upon the cartilages.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|poker}} The [[entitlement]] of the [[player]] to the [[left#Noun|left]] of the [[dealer]] to [[pass#Verb|pass]] the first [[round#Noun|round]] in [[betting#Noun|betting]], and then to come in last or stay out; ''also'', the player holding this position; the [[eldest]] [[hand#Noun|hand]].

====Usage notes====
The age of a person or an animal is often given just as a number, implied to be a number of years. For example "What is the age of your son?" — "Ten." (meaning ten years). With other subjects, units are specified even when years. For example "What is the age of this fossil?" — "Three million years." (not "Three million.")

